# Hej Nathejk — Agent Rules

## Org conventions
Read `.agents/rules/rules.md` for org-wide conventions before proceeding.
Everything in that file applies here unless explicitly overridden below.

---

## This repo

**Purpose:** Nathejk "Hej Nathejk" — in-event companion app (maps, contacts, rulebook, event updates), user-facing frontend with a dedicated api (backend-for-frontend style)
**Group:** Core

### Services

| Service | Technology | Dev target | Local URL |
|---|---|---|---|
| frontend | Vue 3 (TS) | `ui-dev` | `https://hej.local.nathejk.dk` |
| bff | Go | `base` | internal only |

### Key files
- `docker/Dockerfile` — multistage build (dev targets: `ui-dev`, `base`; prod target: `prod`)
- `docker-compose.yml` — dev environment
- `docker-compose.prod.yml` — production stack (plain compose; the org does **not**
  use Swarm — see task 089)
- `roadmap/tasks/TASKS.md` — task board conventions
- `roadmap/prd/` — Product Requirements Documents (see `roadmap/prd/README.md`)

### Frontend skill
Use **`vue3-pwa-layout`** for anything in `vue/`. The older
`vue3-spa-layout-legacy` skill describes the PrimeVue-based sibling repos and
must **not** be applied here.

---

## Repo-specific conventions

- All endpoints must have OpenAPI annotations
- New features and significant changes require a PRD (`prd` skill) before implementation
- **Guardian phone numbers never enter the PWA**, with exactly one exception: a user
  confirming or approving **their own** guardian's number (onboarding / profile —
  PRD 003, PRD 005). No other surface may carry a `phoneParent`: not a directory, not
  a contact list, not a lookup, not a cached manifest. This is a hard rule rather than
  a per-feature judgement, because a guardian's number is the most sensitive field in
  the record and the person it belongs to is not a user of this app and never agreed
  to be in it. If an operational need for one appears, it belongs in an organizer tool
  behind its own decision — not in the participants' app. BFF responses must project
  the field out rather than relying on the client not to render it.
- **Component library:** use [shadcn-vue](https://www.shadcn-vue.com/) for all UI
  components (see the `vue3-pwa-layout` skill). **Prefer a standard shadcn-vue
  component whenever one exists** — only hand-roll a component if nothing in the
  catalogue fits, and note why in a comment. Generated primitives live in
  `vue/src/components/ui/` and are owned source — edit them in place rather than
  wrapping them to patch styling.
  **Do not use PrimeVue.** It is being removed (see PRD 004) and must not be
  reintroduced: no `primevue`, no `@primevue/*`, no Lara/theme presets, no
  PrimeIcons.
- **Styling:** Tailwind **v4**, configured CSS-first in `vue/src/assets/main.css`
  (`@import "tailwindcss"`, `@theme`). Do not reintroduce `tailwind.config.js`.
- **Typography:** all **major headlines use the Nathejk font** — the
  `font-nathejk` utility, backed by `--font-nathejk` (Impact + narrow-bold
  fallbacks) in `vue/src/assets/main.css`. That covers page `<h1>`s, title-level
  section headings and the app bar wordmark; body text and controls stay on the
  system sans stack. Never set a font family in a component.
- **Icons:** use [Lucide](https://lucide.dev/) for all icons across the project
  (frontend `@lucide/vue`), unless a specific instruction says otherwise.
  Do not introduce other icon sets (e.g. PrimeIcons, Font Awesome) for UI icons.
- **Browser baseline:** **iOS/iPadOS Safari 16.4+** and **Chrome 111+** (Android
  equivalent). This is not a constraint we chose for tooling's sake — it is what
  the product already requires: iOS only supports **Web Push for home-screen web
  apps from 16.4**, and the app's core features (service worker, push,
  geolocation, installability) need a modern engine and a secure context anyway.
  Tailwind v4's requirement (Safari 16.4+ / Chrome 111+) lands on exactly the same
  floor, so it costs us no reach. Don't add polyfills or fallbacks for older
  engines; those users cannot use the app's primary features regardless.
